module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Constructions.ProjQuasiCompact
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Constructions.ProjStandardOpenCover
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartKernel.Localization
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjQuotientChartIdeal.Basic
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# A closed subscheme of `Proj` is the `Proj` of the quotient by its ideal of equations

Let `S = ⨁_{n ≥ 0} 𝒮 n` be a graded `R`-algebra with `Proj 𝒮` quasi-compact, and let
`i : Z ⟶ Proj 𝒮` be a closed immersion. Write `I(Z) ⊆ S` for the homogeneous ideal
generated by the homogeneous elements whose canonical twisted global section pulls back to zero
on `Z`. This file proves that the canonical morphism `Proj (𝒮 / I(Z)) ⟶ Proj 𝒮` identifies
`Proj (𝒮 / I(Z))` with `Z`:

`Z ≅ Proj (𝒮 / I(Z))` over `Proj 𝒮`.

Both morphisms are closed immersions into `Proj 𝒮`, so the identification is an equality of
kernel ideal sheaves, and that equality may be checked on a cover by standard opens `D₊(f)`.
Quasi-compactness produces a *finite* such cover whose defining elements share one positive
degree `D`, which is what the chart comparison needs: over `D₊(f)` the section `a / f ^ n` dies on
`Proj (𝒮 / I(Z))` exactly when `f ^ k · a ∈ I(Z)` for some `k`, and it dies on `Z` under exactly
the same condition — one direction is the vanishing of the twisted section of `f ^ k · a`
restricted to `Z`, the other is the saturation step, where one power of `f` is extracted
uniformly from the finitely many charts of the cover. The twists `𝒪(k · D)` that the first
direction needs invertible are invertible because of the cover, with no hypothesis on the
grading.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.ClosedSubschemeProjQuotient.projQuotientIso`: **the isomorphism**
  `Z ≅ Proj (𝒮 / I(Z))`, obtained as the lift of `i` through the closed immersion
  `Stacks.ClosedSubschemeProjQuotient.ambientHom`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ClosedSubschemeProjQuotient.exists_equalDegree_finite_cover`: a quasi-compact `Proj 𝒮`
  is covered by finitely many standard opens of elements of one common positive degree.
* `Stacks.ClosedSubschemeProjQuotient.compactSpace_of_adjoin_degreeOne_eq_top`: over a Noetherian
  graded ring generated in degree one, `Proj 𝒮` is quasi-compact — so the degree-one corollaries
  discharge the hypothesis of the general statements.
* `Stacks.ClosedSubschemeProjQuotient.app_awayMk_eq_zero_iff`: **the chart comparison.** For `f`
  of the cover's degree `d` and `a` homogeneous of degree `n · d`, the section `a / f ^ n` is
  carried to zero by `i` over `D₊(f)` exactly when `f ^ k · a` lies in `I(Z)` for some `k`.
* `Stacks.ClosedSubschemeProjQuotient.saturationIdentification`: the identification of `Z` with
  `Proj (𝒮 / I(Z))` over `Proj 𝒮`, in the packaged form of
  `Stacks.ClosedSubschemeProjQuotient.SaturationIdentification`.
* `Stacks.ClosedSubschemeProjQuotient.ker_eq_ker_ambientHom`: `Z` and `Proj (𝒮 / I(Z))` have the
  same ideal sheaf in `Proj 𝒮`.
* `Stacks.ClosedSubschemeProjQuotient.projQuotientIso_hom_comp_ambientHom`: the isomorphism is
  canonical, i.e. compatible with the two morphisms to `Proj 𝒮`.
* `Stacks.ClosedSubschemeProjQuotient.projQuotientPresentation`: the whole of
  `Stacks.ClosedSubschemeProjQuotient.ProjQuotientPresentation`, whose remaining clause this
  file supplies.
* `Stacks.ClosedSubschemeProjQuotient.projectiveSpace_projQuotientIso`: the case of projective
  space over a Noetherian ring, where quasi-compactness is automatic.

The Noetherian hypothesis enters only through
`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.exists_pow_mul_mem_idealOfClosedSubscheme`, which uses
it to produce a finite family of degree-one elements whose standard opens cover `Proj 𝒮`. Where
such a family is given outright it can be dropped:
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ProjQuotientFiniteCover/Basic.lean` carries the same results with
the family as a hypothesis, and over a polynomial ring — the variables being such a family —
gives Stacks Tag 03GL with no hypothesis on the coefficient ring.

## Implementation notes

Two definitionally equal spellings of the ideal of Stacks Tag 0BXK are in circulation,
`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.idealOfClosedSubscheme` and
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealOfClosedSubscheme.idealOfClosedSubscheme`; the chart material is
stated for the first and the quotient material for the second.
`Stacks.ClosedSubschemeProjQuotient.idealOfClosedSubscheme_eq` records that they agree, by
`rfl`, so no transport is performed anywhere below.

The chart comparison is assembled from the two one-directional statements rather than from
`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.mem_ker_app_basicOpen_iff`, because the form the
reduction consumes names the numerator and the power of `f` separately: the forward direction is
`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.exists_pow_mul_mem_idealOfClosedSubscheme` verbatim,
and the backward direction is
`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.chartFraction_mem_ker_app_of_mem_idealOfClosedSubscheme`
at the numerator `f ^ k · a`, moved back to the numerator `a` by
`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.chartFraction_pow_mul_left`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0801](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0801)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03GL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03GL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BXK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BXK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N1)

## Scope of the tag attribute

Stacks Tag 0801 is about the relative `Proj_S(𝒜)` of a quasi-coherent graded `𝒪_S`-algebra over
an arbitrary base, under the single hypothesis that the structure morphism be quasi-compact. What
carries the tag here is its **absolute case, over an affine base**, which is what the attribute
descriptions name, and under **no hypothesis beyond the tag's own**: over the affine base
`Spec (𝒮 0)` the quasi-compactness of the structure morphism is the quasi-compactness of
`Proj 𝒮`, which is the `[CompactSpace (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒮)]` instance the declarations
carry. In particular neither Noetherianness nor generation in degree one is assumed; both used to
be, and `exists_equalDegree_finite_cover` together with
`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.algebraicGeometry_isInvertible_twistingSheaf_of_cover`
is what replaced them — the first for the finite cover from which a uniform power of `f` is
extracted, the second for invertibility of the twists `𝒪(k · D)` at the multiples of the cover's
common degree, which is exactly the form the source's proof uses.

`projQuotientIso` and `projQuotientIso_hom_comp_ambientHom` also carry Stacks Tag 0BXK, whose
first assertion they are: *if `X = Proj 𝒮` is quasi-compact then every closed subscheme `Z ⊆ X`
has the form `V₊(I(Z))`*, with `I(Z)` the ideal of equations
`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.idealOfClosedSubscheme`. The remaining assertions of
that tag are in `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ProjSaturation/VPlus.lean` (the saturation formula
for `I(V₊(I))` and the characterization of the ideals of the form `I(Z)`) and in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ProjSaturation/WeightedExample.lean` (the counterexample of the
tag's last paragraph).

The relative statement additionally names the quotient `𝒜/ℐ` of a sheaf-level graded algebra by
a graded ideal, which this repository does not yet construct. It needs no monoidal structure and
no internal hom: the multiplication of
`SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra` is a `SheafOfModules.BilinearMap` on sections, and
`Stacks.BilinearMap.extend` — the mechanism behind
`SheafOfModules.PreGradedModule.transfer` — extends a bilinear map into a sheaf along a
degreewise locally bijective map in one variable, so applying it in each variable in turn
descends the multiplication to the degreewise sheafified quotient. The graded ideals are
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal.GradedIdeal`.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace Opposite
open AlgebraicGeometry
open AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj

universe u

namespace Stacks.ClosedSubschemeProjQuotient

variable {R S : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] (𝒮 : ℕ → Submodule R S)
  [GradedAlgebra 𝒮]

/-- The two spellings of the homogeneous ideal of equations of a closed subscheme of `Proj 𝒮`
agree: they are the same span of the same set of homogeneous elements. -/
theorem idealOfClosedSubscheme_eq {Z : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ Proj 𝒮) [IsClosedImmersion i] :
    idealOfClosedSubscheme 𝒮 i =
      Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealOfClosedSubscheme.idealOfClosedSubscheme 𝒮 i :=
  rfl

/-! ### The covering family and the twists it makes invertible -/

/-- **A quasi-compact `Proj 𝒮` is covered by finitely many standard opens of homogeneous elements
of one common positive degree.** This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.exists_common_degree_finite_basicOpen_cover` at the open `⊤`, with the
covering family re-indexed by the `Finset` it produces.

The common degree is what the chart comparison below needs: the localization step compares two
charts `D₊(f)` and `D₊(h)` through the degree-zero fraction `f / h`, which exists only when `f`
and `h` have the same degree. -/
theorem exists_equalDegree_finite_cover [CompactSpace (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒮)] :
    ∃ (D : ℕ) (t : Finset S), 0 < D ∧ (∀ g ∈ t, g ∈ 𝒮 D) ∧
      ⨆ j : {x : S // x ∈ t}, Proj.basicOpen 𝒮 (j : S) = ⊤ := by
  obtain ⟨D, hD, t, ht, hcov⟩ :=
    _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.exists_common_degree_finite_basicOpen_cover 𝒮 ⊤
      (by rw [TopologicalSpace.Opens.coe_top]; exact isCompact_univ)
  refine ⟨D, t, hD, ht, ?_⟩
  have hrw : ⨆ j : {x : S // x ∈ t}, Proj.basicOpen 𝒮 (j : S)
      = ⨆ g ∈ t, Proj.basicOpen 𝒮 g ⊓ (⊤ : (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒮).Opens) := by
    simp only [inf_top_eq]
    rw [iSup_subtype']
  rw [hrw, ← hcov]

/-- **Over a Noetherian graded ring generated in degree one, `Proj 𝒮` is quasi-compact.** Finitely
many degree-one elements already generate the irrelevant ideal, so the quasi-compactness criterion
`AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.compactSpace_iff` applies. This is how the degree-one corollaries below
discharge the quasi-compactness hypothesis of the general statements. -/
theorem compactSpace_of_adjoin_degreeOne_eq_top [IsNoetherianRing S]
    (hgen : Algebra.adjoin (𝒮 0) ((𝒮 1 : Set S)) = ⊤) :
    CompactSpace (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒮) :=
  (_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.compactSpace_iff 𝒮).mpr <| by
    obtain ⟨t, ht1, hspan⟩ :=
      AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.exists_finset_degreeOne_span_irrelevant 𝒮 hgen
    refine ⟨t, fun g hg => ⟨1, Nat.one_pos, ht1 g hg⟩, ?_⟩
    rw [← hspan]
    exact Ideal.le_radical

/-- **The chart comparison.** Let `i : Z ⟶ Proj 𝒮` be a closed immersion, let `fam` be a finite
family of homogeneous elements of one positive degree `d` whose standard opens cover `Proj 𝒮`,
and let `f` be homogeneous of that same degree `d`. A degree-zero fraction `a / f ^ n` over
`D₊(f)`, with `a` homogeneous of degree `n · d`, is carried to zero by `i` exactly when some
`f ^ k · a` lies in the homogeneous ideal of equations of `Z`.

The forward implication is the saturation step and the backward one the vanishing of the twisted
section of `f ^ k · a` on `Z`. -/
theorem app_awayMk_eq_zero_iff {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d) {ι : Type*} [Finite ι] (fam : ι → S)
    (hfam : ∀ j, fam j ∈ 𝒮 d) (hcov : ⨆ j, Proj.basicOpen 𝒮 (fam j) = ⊤)
    {Z : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ Proj 𝒮) [IsClosedImmersion i] {f : S} (hf : f ∈ 𝒮 d)
    (n : ℕ) (a : S) (ha : a ∈ 𝒮 (n • d)) :
    (i.app (Proj.basicOpen 𝒮 f)).hom
        ((Proj.awayToSection 𝒮 f).hom (HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk 𝒮 hf n a ha)) = 0 ↔
      ∃ k : ℕ, f ^ k * a ∈ idealOfClosedSubscheme 𝒮 i := by
  refine ⟨fun h => exists_pow_mul_mem_idealOfClosedSubscheme 𝒮 hd fam hfam hcov hf i n
    ⟨a, ha⟩ (RingHom.mem_ker.mpr h), ?_⟩
  rintro ⟨k, hk⟩
  have hmem : f ^ k * a ∈ 𝒮 ((k + n) • d) := by
    have hp := SetLike.mul_mem_graded (SetLike.pow_mem_graded (A := 𝒮) k hf) ha
    rwa [← add_smul] at hp
  have := algebraicGeometry_isInvertible_twistingSheaf_of_cover 𝒮 fam d hfam hcov (k + n)
  have h1 := chartFraction_mem_ker_app_of_mem_idealOfClosedSubscheme 𝒮 hf hd i
    (k + n) ⟨f ^ k * a, hmem⟩ hk
  rw [chartFraction_pow_mul_left 𝒮 hf k n ⟨a, ha⟩ ⟨f ^ k * a, hmem⟩ rfl] at h1
  exact RingHom.mem_ker.mp h1

/-- **A closed subscheme of `Proj 𝒮` is the `Proj` of the quotient by its ideal of equations.**
For `Proj 𝒮` quasi-compact, `Z` is isomorphic over `Proj 𝒮` to `Proj (𝒮 / I(Z))`.

Quasi-compactness produces a finite cover by standard opens of homogeneous elements of one
common positive degree `D`; the chart comparison holds on each of them, and the twists `𝒪(n · D)`
it needs are invertible by the cover alone. -/
@[ega "II 2.9.2" "more general"]
theorem saturationIdentification [CompactSpace (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒮)]
    {Z : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ Proj 𝒮) [IsClosedImmersion i] :
    SaturationIdentification 𝒮 i := by
  obtain ⟨D, t, hD, ht, hcov⟩ := exists_equalDegree_finite_cover 𝒮
  have hfam : ∀ j : {x : S // x ∈ t}, (j : S) ∈ 𝒮 D := fun j => ht _ j.2
  exact Stacks.ProjQuotientChartIdeal.saturationIdentification_of_app_awayMk_eq_ideal 𝒮 i
    (fun j : {x : S // x ∈ t} => (j : S)) (fun _ => D) hfam (fun _ => hD) hcov
    fun j n a ha => app_awayMk_eq_zero_iff 𝒮 hD
      (fun j : {x : S // x ∈ t} => (j : S)) hfam hcov i (hfam j) n a ha

/-- `Z` and `Proj (𝒮 / I(Z))` cut out the same ideal sheaf of `Proj 𝒮`. -/
theorem ker_eq_ker_ambientHom [CompactSpace (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒮)]
    {Z : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ Proj 𝒮) [IsClosedImmersion i] :
    i.ker = (ambientHom 𝒮 i).ker :=
  Stacks.ProjQuotientSaturationKer.ker_eq_of_saturationIdentification 𝒮 i
    (saturationIdentification 𝒮 i)

/-- **The isomorphism `Z ≅ Proj (𝒮 / I(Z))`.** It is the lift of `i` through the closed immersion
`Stacks.ClosedSubschemeProjQuotient.ambientHom`, which is invertible because the two closed
subschemes have the same ideal sheaf. -/
@[stacks 0801 "the absolute case, over an affine base",
  stacks 0BXK "the first assertion: for \
  `X = Proj 𝒮` quasi-compact, every closed subscheme `Z ⊆ X` has the form `V₊(I(Z))`",
  ega "II 2.9.2" "more general"]
def projQuotientIso [CompactSpace (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒮)]
    {Z : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ Proj 𝒮) [IsClosedImmersion i] :
    Z ≅ projQuotient 𝒮 i :=
  haveI : IsClosedImmersion (ambientHom 𝒮 i) := isClosedImmersion_ambientHom 𝒮 i
  haveI : IsIso (IsClosedImmersion.lift (ambientHom 𝒮 i) i
      (ker_eq_ker_ambientHom 𝒮 i).symm.le) :=
    IsClosedImmersion.isIso_lift (ambientHom 𝒮 i) i (ker_eq_ker_ambientHom 𝒮 i).symm
  asIso (IsClosedImmersion.lift (ambientHom 𝒮 i) i (ker_eq_ker_ambientHom 𝒮 i).symm.le)

/-- **The isomorphism is canonical**: it is compatible with the two morphisms to `Proj 𝒮`, so it
is an equality of closed subschemes of `Proj 𝒮` and not merely an abstract isomorphism. -/
@[simp, stacks 0801 "the identification is over the ambient Proj; the absolute case, over an \
  affine base", stacks 0BXK "the first assertion: the identification `Z = V₊(I(Z))` is one of \
  closed subschemes of `X = Proj 𝒮`, not merely an abstract isomorphism"]
theorem projQuotientIso_hom_comp_ambientHom [CompactSpace (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒮)]
    {Z : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ Proj 𝒮) [IsClosedImmersion i] :
    (projQuotientIso 𝒮 i).hom ≫ ambientHom 𝒮 i = i :=
  have : IsClosedImmersion (ambientHom 𝒮 i) := isClosedImmersion_ambientHom 𝒮 i
  IsClosedImmersion.lift_fac (ambientHom 𝒮 i) i (ker_eq_ker_ambientHom 𝒮 i).symm.le

/-- **The presentation of a closed subscheme of `Proj 𝒮` as a `Proj`**, with every clause
discharged: the quotient by the ideal of equations is degreewise surjective with the expected
kernel, its `Proj` is a closed subscheme of `Proj 𝒮`, and it is `Z`. -/
def projQuotientPresentation [CompactSpace (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒮)]
    {Z : Scheme.{u}} (i : Z ⟶ Proj 𝒮) [IsClosedImmersion i] :
    ProjQuotientPresentation 𝒮 i where
  quotient_epi := surjective_quotientMk 𝒮 i
  quotient_kernel := quotientMk_coe_eq_zero_iff 𝒮 i
  isClosedImmersion_ambient := isClosedImmersion_ambientHom 𝒮 i
  iso := projQuotientIso 𝒮 i
  iso_over_ambient := projQuotientIso_hom_comp_ambientHom 𝒮 i

section ProjectiveSpace

attribute [local instance] MvPolynomial.gradedAlgebra

variable (R' : Type u) [CommRing R'] (e : ℕ)

/-- **A closed subscheme of projective space is the `Proj` of the quotient by its homogeneous
ideal.** Over a Noetherian ring, the hypothesis that the grading be generated in degree one is
automatic for a polynomial ring. -/
@[ega "II 2.9.2" "(ii), special case"]
def projectiveSpace_projQuotientIso [IsNoetherianRing R'] {Z : Scheme.{u}}
    (i : Z ⟶ Proj (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin e) R')) [IsClosedImmersion i] :
    Z ≅ projQuotient (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin e) R') i :=
  haveI : CompactSpace (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj
      (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin e) R')) :=
    compactSpace_of_adjoin_degreeOne_eq_top _
      (MvPolynomial.adjoin_homogeneousSubmodule_one_eq_top (Fin e) R')
  projQuotientIso _ i

end ProjectiveSpace

end Stacks.ClosedSubschemeProjQuotient

end
